  "aboutWhatTitle": "What this app does",
  "aboutWhatBody": "Records all night and identifies, entirely on your phone, what kinds of sounds you made — snoring, breathing, coughing, talking in your sleep, moving around, background noise — then lays out a timeline and the numbers for that night.",
  "aboutPrivacyTitle": "Your data stays on the phone by default",
  "aboutPrivacySubtitle": "All analysis happens on the device",
  "aboutPrivacyBody": "Nothing is uploaded by default: all analysis happens on the device, and the raw audio is discarded right after — all that is kept is when each sound happened and what it was (plus the snore and airway-signal clips if you left the switch above on).\n\nThe one exception is if you set up Nutstore / WebDAV yourself on the Export page — after that, each night uploads to your own cloud. This app has no server of its own.",
  "aboutNotTitle": "What it isn't",
  "aboutNotBody": "It is not a medical device and cannot diagnose sleep apnoea or anything else. The results come from a general-purpose audio event model that has never been calibrated to you specifically. If something feels wrong, see a doctor.",
